The code statements that lead to the bug are:
if (!is_polling(sdd)) {
    dma_release_channel(sdd->rx_dma.ch);
    dma_release_channel(sdd->tx_dma.ch);
}
Reason:
A prior commit moved DMA channel allocation from probe() to s3c64xx_spi_prepare_transfer(), but the remove() function was not updated. These leftover deallocation calls attempt to release DMA channels that are either not allocated (still NULL) or already freed during driver unbind. Dereferencing NULL channel pointers leads to a NULL-pointer dereference.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
-	if (!is_polling(sdd)) {
-		dma_release_channel(sdd->rx_dma.ch);
-		dma_release_channel(sdd->tx_dma.ch);
-	}
Reason:
Removing this code from s3c64xx_spi_remove() ensures that the driver no longer tries to release DMA channels during unbind. Since channel allocation now happens only in s3c64xx_spi_prepare_transfer() (and is undone after each transfer), there is no need to release channels in remove(). This eliminates the NULL-dereference on driver unbind.

